### Preserve thumbnail fallback during previewer reuse

**Severity:** `medium`

When a reused image previewer fails to decode the next file at full quality, `Preview` can still contain the previous image. Checking `Preview is null` therefore skips the cached-thumbnail fallback and sends otherwise previewable files to the error path. Attempt the thumbnail fallback whenever the full-quality load fails; the double buffer keeps the old frame visible until the replacement is ready.

```suggestion
            if (!loaded)
            {
                loaded = await LoadThumbnailAsync(cancellationToken);
            }
```

### Do not publish stale image dimensions after navigation

**Severity:** `medium`

The size lookup runs on a background task and can finish after navigation has canceled the request. Updating `ImageSize` without rechecking cancellation lets an older request overwrite the dimensions used by the current preview, causing incorrect scaling. Check cancellation immediately after the await and before mutating the shared properties.

```suggestion
            cancellationToken.ThrowIfCancellationRequested();

            if (State == PreviewState.Loaded)
            {
                ImageSize = size;
            }
```
